  "history": "National Highway 67 runs from the port of Krishnapatnam on the Andhra coast, through Nellore, Proddatur and Tadipatri, into Karnataka at Ballari and on through Hosapete to Hubballi. It is an ore road: the iron ore of the Ballari region and the granite and cement of Rayalaseema move along it towards the ports. It also passes within a few kilometres of Hampi.",
  "facts": [
    "Runs from Krishnapatnam port on the Bay of Bengal to Hubballi in northern Karnataka.",
    "Passes Hosapete, the gateway town for the ruins of Hampi, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.",
    "Carries iron ore from the Ballari mining belt towards the coast.",
    "Crosses the dry Rayalaseema districts, some of the least rained-on country in peninsular India."
  ],
  "significance": "It is the main road link between the mineral belt of northern Karnataka and the ports of coastal Andhra Pradesh, and it carries a heavy load of ore and cement.",
